<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan grains/oilseeds tender results in August.</title>
<headline>Taiwan grains/oilseeds tender results in August.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan interests bought during August a total of 432,000 tonnes U.S. soybeans and 113,470 tonnes of U.S. wheat at tenders.</p>
<p>Basic information of August soybean/corn tender results:</p>
<p>(Prices based on US$ per tonne)</p>
<p> Date Buyer Tonne  Type  Delivery	Seller Price/Freight</p>
<p> 29  BSPA  54,000  soy   Nov11-15	Bunge  $.8584/Jan/CNF</p>
<p> 29  BSPA  54,000  soy   Dec 6-20	Cargil $.8787/Jan/CNF</p>
<p> 23  BSPA  54,000  soy   Nov10-24	Zennoh $.8570/Jan/CNF</p>
<p>	     54,000  soy   Dec 5-19	Agrex  $.8980/Jan/CNF</p>
<p> 13  BSPA  54,000  soy   Sept22-Oct 6  Contin $.9630/Jan/CNF</p>
<p>	     54,000  soy   Oct16-30	Contin $.8860/Jan/CNF</p>
<p>  8  BSPA  54,000  soy   Sept22-Oct 6  Contin $.9950/Jan/CNF</p>
<p>	     54,000  soy   Oct16-30	Bunge  $.9020/Jan/CNF</p>
<p>Delivery periods for soybean and corn shipments are stated for the U.S. Gulf. Shipments from the Pacific Northwest are 15 days after the Gulf.  </p>
<p>Basic information of recent wheat tender results:</p>
<p>	 (Prices based on US$ per tonne)</p>
<p> Date Buyer Tonne  Type  Delivery	Seller Price/Freight</p>
<p> 29  Flour		   Sept10-30			  FOB $20.4</p>
<p>     Mill   16,300 DNS			Mitsui $212.00</p>
<p>     Assoc   7,000 HRW			Mitsui $205.10</p>
<p>		 2,700  WW			 Louis $202.65</p>
<p> 29  Flour		   Sept20-Oct 10		    FOB $19.4</p>
<p>     Mill   19,500 DNS		     Cargil $212.25</p>
<p>     Assoc  10,000 HRW		     Contin $204.74</p>
<p>		 4,500  WW		     Louis  $199.71</p>
<p> 29  Flour		   Sept25-Oct 20		    FOB $19.4</p>
<p>     Mill    23,500 DNS		     Cargil $212.25</p>
<p>     Assoc    9,600 HRW		     Contin $204.74</p>
<p>		  4,900  WW		     Cargil $199.56</p>
<p> 28  Food    7,700 HRW   Sept 10-30    Agrex  $204.75 FOB</p>
<p>     Bureau  7,770  SW   Sept 10-30    Agrex  $193.75 FOB</p>
<p>August wheat tenders included Dark Northern Spring (DNS), Hard Red Winter (HRW), White Wheat (WW) and Soft Wheat (SW). Wheat shipments all are slated for delivery from the Pacific Northwest.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
